WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:03.300
Important, not urgent: defending the work that builds a career.

2
00:00:03.700 --> 00:00:09.110
Friday, six in the evening. Rani has been busy all week. She answered every ping and joined every meeting.

3
00:00:09.510 --> 00:00:15.430
And nothing that matters has moved. Her certification practice got zero hours. Urgency is a sensation, not a measure of value.

4
00:00:15.830 --> 00:00:23.790
Sort any week into four boxes. Urgent and important: real deadlines. Important, not urgent: practice, planning, people, health. Careers are built here. Urgent, not important: most pings. And neither.

5
00:00:24.190 --> 00:00:30.210
The trap: box three dresses up as box one, and eats the hours box two needed.

6
00:00:30.610 --> 00:00:38.510
The defence is a weekly preview. Twenty minutes, three moves. Review where you are going. Put two or three important blocks in the calendar first. Then preview the known deadlines.

7
00:00:38.910 --> 00:00:47.100
A calendar block needs one more defence: a rehearsed no, not a fake maybe. A graceful no has three parts: thanks, the reason you are protecting, and an alternative.

8
00:00:47.500 --> 00:00:52.730
The next Thursday, seven in the evening. The pings still arrive. The block holds.

9
00:00:53.130 --> 00:01:00.130
Every yes is an unpriced no to something else. Price it before you give it.

10
00:01:00.530 --> 00:01:04.930
Now it is your turn. Book twenty minutes this weekend for your first weekly preview.
